---
import Layout from "@/layouts/main.astro";
---

<Layout 
  title="Privacy Policy (Draft) - RS Prints"
  description="Privacy policy, user data collection rules, cookie usage, GDPR/CCPA rights, and data protection terms."
  canonicalUrl="/privacy-policy"
  currentActive="privacy"
>
  <main class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8 md:py-12 max-w-4xl flex-1 flex flex-col gap-8">
    <!-- Header Section -->
    <div class="border-b border-border pb-6">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider bg-amber-500/15 text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 border border-amber-500/30">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3Z"/>
            <line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/>
            <line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/>
          </svg>
          Dummy / Placeholder Document
        </span>
        <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground font-mono">
          Last updated: February 13, 2026 (Draft)
        </span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-2 leading-relaxed">
        Learn how we handle, collect, safeguard, and process your personal data and protect your privacy rights.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Dummy Flag / Draft Notice Banner -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 dark:bg-amber-950/20 p-4 md:p-5 flex gap-4 text-amber-950 dark:text-amber-200">
      <div class="shrink-0 mt-0.5">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
          <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/>
          <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-1 text-xs md:text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">
          Notice: Placeholder / Sample Document (Pending Formal Execution)
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          This Privacy Policy is an illustrative draft template prepared for staging, demonstration, and layout purposes. All original third-party brand names, domains, and entity identifiers have been sanitized and replaced with standardized placeholders (e.g., <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-foreground">[Company Name]</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-foreground">[https://yourwebsite.com]</code>). This draft is subject to formal customization and legal validation prior to final adoption.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Privacy Policy Content -->
    <div class="text-xs md:text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground space-y-8 font-sans">
      
      <!-- Introduction & Scope -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <p>
          At <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span>, accessible from <span class="text-primary font-medium">[https://yourwebsite.com]</span>, one of our main priorities is the privacy of our visitors. This Privacy Policy document outlines the categories of information that are collected and recorded by <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> and explains how we handle, process, and protect it.
        </p>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy applies solely to our online activities and is valid for visitors to our website with respect to the information that they share and/or collect on <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[https://yourwebsite.com]</span>. This policy is not applicable to any information collected offline or via channels other than this website.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you have additional questions or require further information regarding our privacy practices, please contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@yourdomain.com" class="text-primary hover:underline font-mono">[privacy@yourdomain.com]</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 1: Consent -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>1.</span> Consent
        </h2>
        <p>
          By accessing and using our website, you hereby consent to our Privacy Policy and agree to the collection and handling of your data in accordance with its terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Information We Collect -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>2.</span> Information We Collect
        </h2>
        <p>
          The personal information that you are asked to provide, and the reasons why you are asked to provide it, will be made clear to you at the point of request:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-foreground">Direct Inquiries & Customer Support:</strong> If you contact us directly via email, contact forms, or phone, we may receive additional information about you such as your name, email address, phone number, delivery address, the contents of your message, any design file attachments or images you provide, and any other details you choose to share.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-foreground">Account Registration & Ordering:</strong> When you register for an Account or place a customized print order, we may collect your contact and billing details, including your full name, business or entity name, shipping address, billing address, phone number, and email address.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-foreground">Custom Artwork & Uploaded Graphics:</strong> Photos, graphics, logos, and custom printing specifications provided by you to fulfill personalized print merchandise orders.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: How We Use Your Information -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>3.</span> How We Use Your Information
        </h2>
        <p>
          We utilize the information collected for various legitimate business purposes, including to:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Provide, operate, manufacture, and maintain our products and website;</li>
          <li>Process customer transactions, custom merchandise printing, and manage shipments;</li>
          <li>Improve, personalize, optimize, and expand our website user experience;</li>
          <li>Understand and analyze how visitors interact with our website and product catalogs;</li>
          <li>Develop new customized print offerings, services, features, and site capabilities;</li>
          <li>Communicate with you directly or through our authorized customer service partners to provide order updates, delivery tracking, and transactional notices;</li>
          <li>Send administrative notices, order confirmation emails, and optional marketing promotions (subject to your opt-out preferences);</li>
          <li>Detect, mitigate, and prevent fraudulent transactions, spam, and security incidents.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Log Files -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>4.</span> Log Files & Analytics
        </h2>
        <p>
          <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> follows a standard procedure of utilizing server log files. These files log visitors when they access websites. All hosting providers perform this as part of standard infrastructure hosting analytics.
        </p>
        <p>
          Information collected by log files includes internet protocol (IP) addresses, browser type, Internet Service Provider (ISP), date and time stamps, referring/exit pages, and click counts. This data is not linked to any personally identifiable information and is used exclusively for evaluating visitor trends, administering the site, tracking aggregate movements, and gathering demographic statistics.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Third-Party Privacy Policies & Cookies -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>5.</span> Third-Party Privacy Policies & Cookies
        </h2>
        <p>
          <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span>’s Privacy Policy does not apply to external advertisers, payment gateways, logistics partners, or linked websites. We strongly advise consulting the respective privacy policies of these third-party services for comprehensive information regarding their data practices and opt-out procedures.
        </p>
        <p>
          You have the ability to disable or manage cookies via your individual browser settings. Detailed guidance on cookie management across specific web browsers can be reviewed at your browser's official support documentation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6: CCPA Privacy Rights -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>6.</span> CCPA Privacy Rights (Do Not Sell My Personal Information)
        </h2>
        <p>
          Under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and equivalent privacy frameworks, consumers have specific statutory protections, including:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>The right to request that a business disclose the categories and specific pieces of personal data collected about consumers;</li>
          <li>The right to request that a business delete any personal data collected about the consumer;</li>
          <li>The right to request that a business that sells a consumer's personal data does not sell that consumer's personal data (we do not sell user personal data).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you submit a verifiable request, we will respond within one (1) month. To exercise any of these statutory rights, please reach out to us at our designated privacy contact.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 7: GDPR Data Protection Rights -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>7.</span> GDPR Data Protection Rights
        </h2>
        <p>
          We are committed to ensuring you are fully cognizant of all your data protection entitlements. Every qualifying user is entitled to:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li><strong class="text-foreground">The right to access:</strong> You have the right to request copies of your personal data records.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-foreground">The right to rectification:</strong> You have the right to request correction of inaccurate data or completion of incomplete information.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-foreground">The right to erasure:</strong> You have the right to request deletion of your personal data, subject to statutory record-keeping constraints.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-foreground">The right to restrict processing:</strong> You have the right to request restriction on how your personal data is processed under qualifying conditions.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-foreground">The right to object to processing:</strong> You have the right to object to our processing of your personal data under certain conditions.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-foreground">The right to data portability:</strong> You have the right to request the transfer of your collected data to another organization or directly to you in a structured format.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Upon receiving a request, we have thirty (30) days to furnish a response. If you wish to exercise any of these rights, please contact our privacy compliance desk.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 8: Children's Information -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>8.</span> Protection of Children's Information
        </h2>
        <p>
          Protecting minors while using the internet is a fundamental priority. We encourage parents and guardians to monitor, participate in, and guide their children's online browsing.
        </p>
        <p>
          <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> does not knowingly collect any personally identifiable information from children under the age of 13. If you believe that your child has inadvertently provided personal information on our website, we urge you to contact us immediately, and we will take expeditious measures to promptly purge such data from our records.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 9: Privacy Contact & Grievances -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>9.</span> Privacy Contact & Inquiries
        </h2>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-card/60 space-y-1.5 text-xs md:text-sm">
          <p><span class="font-semibold text-foreground">Data Privacy Desk:</span> [Privacy & Compliance Team]</p>
          <p><span class="font-semibold text-foreground">Email:</span> <a href="mailto:privacy@yourdomain.com" class="text-primary hover:underline font-mono">[privacy@yourdomain.com]</a></p>
          <p><span class="font-semibold text-foreground">Mailing Address:</span> [Registered Office Address, City, State, PIN Code, Country]</p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
